From 55a71946d97410f850b19637d4590ef7999a17c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:14:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] plugin: bound every RPC and give ADD/DEL overall budgets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CNI commands used unbounded contexts and non-blocking dials, so a wedged
meshnetd, API server or remote daemon stalled kubelet's CNI ADD (and with
it containerd's CRI workers) indefinitely — the sandbox-creation wedge
observed under bringup bursts.

- dialGRPC: bounded blocking dial (30s) plus a unary interceptor giving
  every RPC its own 30s timeout under the caller's overall budget; adopted
  for the local daemon dials, the remote-VTEP update dial and both
  grpc-wire dials in grpcwires-plugin.go (with the underlying dial errors
  finally included in the messages).
- cmdAdd runs under a 90s overall budget and decorates deadline-exceeded
  failures with the pod identity and budget.
- cmdDel runs under a best-effort 45s budget: on expiry the error is logged
  and DEL returns success, so pod teardown is never blocked by meshnet
  cleanup; leftover state is reconciled by the next ADD.

Upstreamable.
